  "narrative": "**Biological narrative — metabolomics findings**\n\nThe strongest signal in this dataset is a coordinated perturbation of **eicosanoid synthesis** (Wikipathways WP167; FDR ≈ 0, fold-enrichment ≈ 1000×), with five metabolites — arachidonic acid (C00219), leukotriene A4 (C00909), 15-HETE (C04742), 15-deoxy-Δ¹²,¹⁴-PGJ2 (C14717), and 5-HETE (C04805) — all hitting this pathway simultaneously.\n\n**Key driver compounds.** Arachidonic acid (C00219) is the primary upstream precursor: KEGG reaction-graph analysis confirms it is reachable in two enzymatic steps from leukotriene A4 (C00909) and 5-HETE (C04805) via the common intermediate C05356, and in two steps to 15-HETE (C04742). This positions arachidonic acid as the upstream driver whose altered abundance can cascade into multiple downstream eicosanoid effectors. Leukotriene A4 (C00909) and the HETE species (C04742, C04805) represent the branching lipoxygenase and non-enzymatic oxidative arms of this network, while 15-deoxy-Δ¹²,¹⁴-PGJ2 (C14717) reflects cycloxygenase-mediated processing.\n\n**Upstream/downstream relationships verified.** Using directed BFS over the KEGG reaction graph:\n- Arachidonic acid → Leukotriene A4 (bidirectional, 2 hops via C05356).\n- Arachidonic acid → 15-HETE (forward, 2 hops).\n- Arachidonic acid → 5-HETE (forward, 2 hops).\n\nThese findings collectively suggest that the treatment condition drives preferential shunting of the arachidonic acid pool toward the lipoxygenase and cycloxygenase branches, consistent with an inflammatory or oxidative-stress stimulus. The parallel elevation of leukotriene A4, 15-HETE, and 5-HETE alongside 15-deoxy-Δ¹²,¹⁴-PGJ2 indicates simultaneous activation of both LOX and COX pathways, which may reflect a self-amplifying eicosanoid storm. The simultaneous elevation of histamines and gentisic acid may further modulate the vascular and analgesic context of this response.",
